---
import ContentLayout from '@/layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@lib/site';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What we collect, why, and how to opt out. Cookieless analytics always; marketing pixels only with consent where required."
  h1="Privacy policy"
  updated="2026-09-28"
  toc={[
    { id: 'collect', label: 'What we collect' },
    { id: 'analytics', label: 'Analytics & advertising' },
    { id: 'email', label: 'Email' },
    { id: 'uploads', label: 'Photos you upload' },
    { id: 'payments', label: 'Payments' },
    { id: 'rights', label: 'Your choices' },
    { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    [EDIT: have a lawyer review before launch.] {site.dealerName} (“we”) runs this site. This policy
    explains what we collect and why, in plain language.
  </p>
  <section id="collect" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Forms:</strong> the information you type into the waitlist, trade, contact, request,
        notify, return, and review forms, plus the page you were on and any campaign tags in the
        link you arrived from.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Orders:</strong> name, email, phone, shipping address, and what you bought, received
        from Stripe after checkout.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local preferences:</strong> your cart, wishlist, unit preference (ft/cm), and
        dismissed notices are stored in your browser only and never sent to us.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section id="analytics" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Analytics &amp; advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless and does not track you across sites. We
      may also use Google Analytics 4 and the Meta Pixel with server-side Conversions API to measure
      ads. These load only after you interact with the page, never when your browser sends a Global
      Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, and, where a consent banner is shown, only if you
      allow it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="email" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      Joining the drop list adds you to our list at [EMAIL PROVIDER]. Every email has an unsubscribe
      link and our postal address, as the CAN-SPAM Act requires. Order emails come from Stripe and
      from us and are transactional.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="uploads" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Photos you upload</h2>
    <p>
      Room photos and review photos are stored in Cloudflare R2. We strip location and camera
      metadata from JPEG and PNG files on upload. Room photos are used only to make your mockup and
      are deleted on request. Review photos are shown publicly only after you submit a review and we
      approve it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="payments" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Checkout is handled by Stripe. We never see or store your card number. Stripe’s privacy policy
      applies to the payment itself.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="rights" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Email us to see, correct, or delete what we hold about you. We answer within 10 business days.
      We do not sell personal information.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.dealerName}, {site.address}. <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
